Thread A runs `worker.run()`. A second later, thread B calls `worker.stop()`. What does the Java Memory Model guarantee?

```java
class Worker implements Runnable {
    private boolean running = true;

    public void run() {
        long spins = 0;
        while (running) {
            spins++;
        }
        System.out.println("stopped after " + spins);
    }

    public void stop() { running = false; }
}
